# mypy
.mypy_cache/

# Real ticket validation numbers for the lab ticket authority. They identify
# tickets issued by a real property, so they are operational data: keep them
# local. lab_tickets.example.json carries placeholders and is committed.
lab_tickets.json

# Derived from survey/*.json by examples/survey_store.py. Regenerate it
# rather than committing a binary that grows with every survey.
survey/*.sqlite3
survey/survey.log
survey/.survey-seq
survey/.no-poweroff

# Any SQLite database is derived -- rebuild it from the JSONs or the poller.
*.sqlite3

# -- found by deploy/mirror_to_public.py's "not in either list" report on the
# -- lab gateway, 2026-11-02. All four sat untracked and UNIGNORED, so a plain
# -- `git add -A` would have committed them.

# SQLite's sidecar files. "*.sqlite3" above does NOT match these: the suffix
# comes AFTER the extension. The -wal in particular holds committed
# transactions not yet folded into the database -- real meter rows and events,
# 4 MB of them when this was found.
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.sqlite3-journal

# A ticket file under a name the rule above does not catch: "lab_tickets.json"
# is a literal, and this is not it. Same contents, same reason.
tickets.json

# ...and neither does it catch lab_tickets.json.bak, which
# examples/ticket_file_add.py writes itself every time it edits the file. Found
# as the only untracked file on the gateway, 2026-11-03. "lab_tickets.json*"
# does NOT match lab_tickets.example.json, which stays committed.
lab_tickets.json*

# Any editor or tool backup. Same contents as whatever it backs up, and the
# same reason not to commit it.
*.bak

# Handpay queue dumps from examples/handpay_queue_drain.py: amounts, levels
# and reset ids read off a real cabinet.
handpay-queue-*.json
survey/screens/
survey/screens/
survey/screens/
survey/screens/
